## Sister project of the research wiki

This project is registered as a sister of the **research wiki / second brain** at `{{second_brain_path}}`.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Project name | `{{project_name}}` |
| Type | `{{type}}` |
| Group | `{{group}}` |
| Domain | `{{domain}}` |
| Auto-connect | `{{auto_connect}}` |
| Sister entry | [{{sister_projects_yaml_entry_url}}]({{sister_projects_yaml_entry_url}}) |

**Connection mechanism**: `python3 -m tools.setup --connect-project /root` from inside the second brain installs:
- `research-wiki` MCP server entry in `/root/.mcp.json`
- `tools/gateway.py` forwarder (so `python3 -m tools.gateway orient` works from inside this project)
- `tools/view.py` forwarder (so `python3 -m tools.view spine` etc. works)
- A `## Second Brain Connection` block appended to `AGENTS.md`

**Bidirectional flow:**
- This project consumes from the second brain: methodology, standards, validated lessons, patterns, sister-project syntheses (e.g. Suricata, PolarProxy, Hanke integration).
- This project contributes to the second brain: lessons learned, patterns observed, decisions made — via `python3 -m tools.gateway contribute --type lesson --title "..."`.

For per-session orientation: `python3 -m tools.gateway orient`. For methodology + adoption guide: see the second brain's `wiki/spine/references/adoption-guide.md`.
